
# machine translated (Spanish), not yet reviewed by a person.

# Said in red under the Bluetooth switch when switching it on failed for no known reason.
settings-bluetooth-on-failed = No se pudo activar el Bluetooth.

# Said in red under the Bluetooth switch when switching it off failed for no known reason.
settings-bluetooth-off-failed = No se pudo desactivar el Bluetooth.

# Said in red when Bluetooth refuses something because it is not switched on; the first sentence says what could not be done.
settings-bluetooth-cause-not-ready = { $could_not } El Bluetooth no está activado.

# Said in red when the PIN or number typed was wrong; the first sentence says what could not be done.
settings-bluetooth-cause-auth-failed = { $could_not } No se aceptó el PIN o el número. Inténtalo de nuevo.

# Said in red when the pairing was turned down; the first sentence says what could not be done.
settings-bluetooth-cause-turned-down = { $could_not } Se rechazó, aquí o en el otro dispositivo.

# Said in red when the other device did not answer in time; the first sentence says what could not be done.
settings-bluetooth-cause-timeout = { $could_not } El otro dispositivo no respondió a tiempo. Ponlo en modo de emparejamiento e inténtalo de nuevo.

# Said in red when the same thing is already being done; the first sentence says what could not be done.
settings-bluetooth-cause-in-progress = { $could_not } Ya se está haciendo. Espera un momento.

# Said in red when the device did not answer; the first sentence says what could not be done.
settings-bluetooth-cause-no-answer = { $could_not } El dispositivo no respondió. Comprueba que esté encendido y cerca, e inténtalo de nuevo.

# Said in red when the device is not ready to be used; the first sentence says what could not be done.
settings-bluetooth-cause-not-available = { $could_not } El dispositivo no está listo para usarse. Ponlo en modo de emparejamiento e inténtalo de nuevo.

# The word for the system bus in "The system bus is not available".
settings-bluetooth-the-bus = El bus del sistema

# Headline of the page while Bluetooth is looked for.
settings-bluetooth-top-looking = Buscando Bluetooth…

# Headline of the page when the Bluetooth service is not running.
settings-bluetooth-top-gone = El Bluetooth no se está ejecutando en este equipo.

# Headline of the page when Bluetooth is off.
settings-bluetooth-top-off = El Bluetooth está desactivado.

# Headline of the page when Bluetooth is off at a switch or key on the computer itself.
settings-bluetooth-top-hard = El Bluetooth está apagado en el propio equipo.

# Headline of the page when the computer has no Bluetooth.
settings-bluetooth-top-none = Este equipo no tiene Bluetooth.

# Headline of the page when Bluetooth is on and searching.
settings-bluetooth-top-searching = Activado, buscando dispositivos cercanos…

# Headline of the page when Bluetooth is on and nothing is connected.
settings-bluetooth-top-idle = Activado, sin nada conectado por ahora.

# Headline of the page when Bluetooth is on and devices are connected; the names are already joined into a list.
settings-bluetooth-top-connected =
    { $n ->
        [one] Activado, y { $names } está conectado.
        [many] Activado, y { $names } están conectados.
       *[other] Activado, y { $names } están conectados.
    }

# Help text (i button) of the Bluetooth card.
settings-bluetooth-card-about = El interruptor activa o desactiva el Bluetooth de este equipo; debajo está el nombre del adaptador. Mientras Visible para otros dispositivos esté activado, los dispositivos cercanos pueden encontrar este equipo.

# Heading of the Bluetooth card, of its switch's line, and the name of its switch.
settings-bluetooth-title = Bluetooth

# Small line under the Bluetooth switch when Bluetooth is blocked by the system.
settings-bluetooth-switched-off = Apagado.

# SAFETY: needs a human review before it ships
# Heading of the line with the switch that makes this computer visible, and the name of that switch.
settings-bluetooth-visible = Visible para otros dispositivos

# Small line under the Visible to other devices switch.
settings-bluetooth-visible-sub = Los dispositivos cercanos pueden encontrar este equipo.

# Heading of the card when Bluetooth is off at a switch on the computer itself.
settings-bluetooth-hard-line = Apagado en el propio equipo

# Small line under it.
settings-bluetooth-hard-line-sub = Por un interruptor o una tecla. Enciéndelo primero.

# Heading of the card when the computer has no Bluetooth adapter.
settings-bluetooth-no-adapter = Sin adaptador Bluetooth

# Help text (i button) of that card.
settings-bluetooth-no-adapter-about = No se encontró ningún adaptador Bluetooth en este equipo. Uno que se conecte a un puerto USB aparece aquí en cuanto se conecta.

# Line in that card.
settings-bluetooth-none-found = No se encontró ninguno

# Small line under it.
settings-bluetooth-none-found-sub = Uno USB aparece aquí en cuanto se conecta.

# Shown beside the Bluetooth switch while the password is asked for.
settings-bluetooth-waiting = Esperando la contraseña...

# Said in red when this computer could not be made visible to other devices.
settings-bluetooth-visible-failed = No se pudo hacer visible este equipo para otros dispositivos.

# Said in red when this computer could not be hidden from other devices.
settings-bluetooth-hidden-failed = No se pudo ocultar este equipo de otros dispositivos.

# Shown on the two device lists while Bluetooth is off.
settings-bluetooth-switch-on-first = Activa el Bluetooth para usar esto.

# Line in the My devices card when nothing is paired.
settings-bluetooth-none-paired = Aún no hay ninguno emparejado

# Small line under it.
settings-bluetooth-none-paired-sub = Busca dispositivos para emparejar uno.

# Heading of the card that lists paired devices.
settings-bluetooth-mine = Mis dispositivos

# Help text (i button) of the My devices card.
settings-bluetooth-mine-about = Dispositivos emparejados con este equipo, cada uno con su batería cuando la indica. Los conectados al abrir la página van primero, y una línea no se mueve mientras la página esté abierta. Los botones redondos conectan o desconectan uno; la papelera lo olvida, así que habría que emparejarlo de nuevo.

# Line in the Nearby card while the search runs.
settings-bluetooth-looking = Buscando dispositivos...

# Tip of the button that stops the search.
settings-bluetooth-stop-looking = Dejar de buscar

# Heading of the line that starts the search, and tip of its button.
settings-bluetooth-look = Buscar dispositivos

# Small line under it.
settings-bluetooth-look-sub = Pon primero el otro en modo de emparejamiento.

# Heading of the card that lists devices nearby.
settings-bluetooth-nearby = Cercanos

# Help text (i button) of the Nearby card.
settings-bluetooth-nearby-about = Pulsa Buscar dispositivos, pon el otro dispositivo en modo de emparejamiento y pulsa Emparejar junto a él. Los dispositivos cercanos se listan primero por intensidad al abrir la página, y cada uno nuevo se añade al final. Algunos muestran un número para comparar con el de aquí, y otros piden un PIN, que suele estar en sus instrucciones, o 0000.

# Said in red when the search could not be stopped.
settings-bluetooth-stop-failed = No se pudo dejar de buscar dispositivos.

# Said in red when the search could not be started.
settings-bluetooth-start-failed = No se pudo buscar dispositivos.

# Small line of a device that is connected.
settings-bluetooth-connected = Conectado

# Small line of a paired device that is not connected.
settings-bluetooth-not-connected = Sin conexión

# Part of a device's small line: its battery level in per cent.
settings-bluetooth-battery = batería { $n }%

# Tip of the button that pairs a device, and the button of the same name in the pairing question.
settings-bluetooth-pair = Emparejar

# Tip of the button that disconnects a device.
settings-bluetooth-disconnect = Desconectar

# Tip of the button that connects a device.
settings-bluetooth-connect = Conectar

# SAFETY: needs a human review before it ships
# Tip of the bin button that forgets a device.
settings-bluetooth-forget = Olvidar este dispositivo

# Said in red when a device could not be disconnected.
settings-bluetooth-disconnect-failed = No se pudo desconectar.

# Said in red when a device could not be forgotten.
settings-bluetooth-forget-failed = No se pudo olvidar.

# Shown under a device while it is being paired.
settings-bluetooth-pairing = Emparejando...

# Said in red when a device could not be paired.
settings-bluetooth-pair-failed = No se pudo emparejar.

# Shown under a device while it is being connected.
settings-bluetooth-connecting = Conectando...

# Said in red when a device could not be connected.
settings-bluetooth-connect-failed = No se pudo conectar.

# Said under a device that paired but could not be set to connect by itself.
settings-bluetooth-not-trusted = Conectado, pero no se pudo configurar para que se conecte solo la próxima vez. Conéctalo aquí cuando lo quieras.

# Said under a device that shows a code to be typed on it; the code is already written.
settings-bluetooth-type-code = Escribe { $code } en el dispositivo y pulsa Intro en él.

# Question under a device that shows a number to compare with the one on this computer.
settings-bluetooth-compare = ¿El otro dispositivo muestra { $code }?

# SAFETY: needs a human review before it ships
# Tip of the button that answers no to a pairing question.
settings-bluetooth-no = No

# SAFETY: needs a human review before it ships
# Tip of the button that says the numbers match.
settings-bluetooth-yes-matches = Sí, coincide

# SAFETY: needs a human review before it ships
# Question under a device that asks to be paired.
settings-bluetooth-pair-question = ¿Emparejar con este dispositivo?

# Placeholder of the box where a device's PIN is typed.
settings-bluetooth-pin = PIN

# SAFETY: needs a human review before it ships
# Tip of the button that refuses to type a PIN.
settings-bluetooth-cancel = Cancelar

# Help line above the box where a device's PIN is typed.
settings-bluetooth-pin-help = Escribe el PIN de este dispositivo. Suele estar en sus instrucciones, o es 0000.

# Words the settings search looks for on this page (not shown).
settings-bluetooth-keywords = auriculares cascos ratón teclado emparejar dispositivos inalámbrico bluetooth

# Help text at the top of the page.
settings-bluetooth-help = Pulsa Buscar, pon el otro dispositivo en modo de emparejamiento y pulsa Emparejar junto a él.

# Said in red under the Bluetooth switch when restarting the sound service after Bluetooth came back on failed; $why is the system's own reason.
settings-bluetooth-sound-failed = No se pudo reiniciar el sonido Bluetooth, así que los auriculares pueden usar calidad básica hasta que vuelvas a iniciar sesión. { $why }

# Tooltip of the help button beside the Bluetooth switch.
settings-bluetooth-sound-help = Por qué los auriculares suenan básicos después de apagar y encender el Bluetooth



# Said in red when a device is no longer in BlueZ's list; the first sentence says what could not be done.
settings-bluetooth-cause-gone = { $could_not } Ya no se conoce. Búscalo de nuevo.

# Said in red when a paired device's saved pairing is refused; the first sentence says what could not be done.
settings-bluetooth-cause-old-pairing = { $could_not } El emparejamiento guardado ya no se acepta. Olvida el dispositivo y empareja de nuevo.

# Said in red under a device that connected and then dropped at once.
settings-bluetooth-dropped = Se conectó y luego se desconectó. Puede que el emparejamiento guardado esté desactualizado.

# Tooltip of the button that forgets a paired device and looks for it afresh.
settings-bluetooth-pair-again = Olvidar y emparejar de nuevo

# Said under Look for devices after a device was forgotten to be paired afresh.
settings-bluetooth-forgotten-pair = Olvidado. Ponlo en modo de emparejamiento y pulsa Emparejar cuando aparezca abajo.

# Tooltip of the button that opens Help from a failed connection.
settings-bluetooth-more = Más sobre esto

